Reserve the output bound before a secret write is queued

write_secret zeroed the output buffer's current allocation, but a later
request could grow that buffer while the secret was still queued. The
allocator would then free the old allocation, secret included, without
zeroing it. Before a secret enters, the buffer now reserves the whole
capacity its bound allows. Submit already refuses anything past that
bound, so no later request can reallocate it.

output_capacity exposes the allocation for the regression, which fills
the buffer behind a queued secret until the bound refuses a request and
checks that the capacity never changed. Reported in review by
niltempus.
